  "document": "MULTIGRADE RC PAPERS Technical Information (no publication number printed)",
  "date": "2020-10",
  "notes": [
   "The sheet (HARMAN technology Limited, Oct 2020) covers the Multigrade RC range; page 3 has characteristic curves for four emulsions. This sheet traces the one headed 'NEW - MULTIGRADE RC DELUXE & PORTFOLIO' (the older Multigrade IV RC, Warmtone and Cooltone plots on the same page are not traced). Curves are 'exposed through filters 00 - 5. Development MULTIGRADE Dev @1+9. 1 minute at 20 C/68 F.' Densitometry and exposing light are not printed (text only says tungsten or tungsten-halogen enlargers, cold light and LED variable contrast heads).",
   "x axis is RELATIVE log exposure (no lux-seconds): numbers are the printed 0 to 4 scale of each plot. The plot is drawn in two frames: grades 00, 0, 1, 2 and 3 (traced as plot 'curves') and grades 4 and 5 (traced as plot 'curves-grades-4-5'). The two frames have separate x scales (grades 4 and 5 start to rise near 2.0 while grade 3 starts near 1.6), so grade 4/5 positions on the exposure axis must not be compared with grades 00-3. Only whole grades are plotted (no half grades). Density axis: 0 to 2.5 as printed, maximum density about 2.08 for all grades.",
   "Line names: 'grade-00', 'grade-0', 'grade-1', 'grade-2', 'grade-3' ('v' is a copy of grade-3, the grade used for printing), and in the second plot 'grade-4', 'grade-5'. Labels on the sheet: only '3' and '00' (left frame) and '4' and '5' (right frame) are printed; the three middle curves are assigned 0, 1, 2 in order. All five curves of the left frame cross near log exposure 2.0 and density 0.45 (pivot); below it the order is 00 at the top, above it grade 3 is the steepest (leftmost). The curves are less than 0.04 density apart from the toe up to about log exposure 2.4: where they overlap the traced lines follow the centre of the merged ink and the fan of the toe (log exposure 1.5 to 2.0) is placed by assumption, equal spacing between the merged band edges, so differences between grades there are not reliable.",
   "Printed ISO(R) ranges (ISO 6846-1992) for Multigrade RC Deluxe (NEW) at filters 00, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, none: 160, 130, 110, 90, 70, 60, 50, 90. Printed ISO speed (P) at filters 00, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, none: 240, 240, 240, 240, 240, 220, 220, 500; film equivalent ISO about 3-6.",
   "Raster image traced from hand-placed hints. No spectral sensitivity plot and no dye plots exist on this sheet."
  ]
